      "content": "1. Forest Cover & Biodiversity"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "India's National Forest Policy targets maintaining at least 33% of the total geographical area under forest cover.",
        "National Parks offer strict ecosystem protection where human activities like forestry, grazing, and cultivation are prohibited.",
        "Wildlife Sanctuaries provide species-oriented protection with limited permissible human activities subject to permission.",
        "The Environment Protection Act of 1986 was enacted under Article 253 of the Constitution following the Bhopal Gas Tragedy."
      ],
      "id": "95aoypc"
    },
